From aea2d01f4837f32a9502877f02e10f5b8c39165e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:51:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] FEX: own version of D2R's 3D lighting table blur
 (VKD3D_FEX_SHADER_SWAP)

D2R's compute shader 83e2eb4a6bf5f03b blurs a 3D lighting table: for
every cell it sums 2 x A x B filtered samples of one volume, 8,192 per
cell in D2R. On an Adreno 740 one run takes 30 ms with the texture unit
busy all the time, and the game runs it in bursts (up to 19 runs when it
enters an area), which made nearly all of the long frames left in play.

Most of those samples repeat: the first one depends on (i, j, y) only,
the second on (x * A - i * W, j, z). The FEX version (same bindings,
push constants and constant buffer) has each 8 x 8 x 8 group sample
every distinct value of a step once into shared memory and sum from
there, fetching the next step while it sums. Results match the game's
shader up to float rounding (host check on lavapipe over 15 table
sizes: largest relative difference 4e-6).

vkd3d swaps it in after translating the shader, only when the
translation is the SPIR-V the FEX version was written against. A listed
shader is never taken from a pipeline cache, so turning the swap off
can't pick up the FEX version from one. VKD3D_FEX_SHADER_SWAP=0 turns
it off; the gpu report carries a note with the counts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WZVGoVEaHJ78mpf2D3MiER
